  "title": "Principle 2: the brain’s models are never accurate",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "6a504f2c-02e7-4823-baeb-97780e586a3e",
      "text": "The brain builds simplified models of reality that can be computed fast and cheaply, as color simplifies a reflectance spectrum and the body schema simplifies the body. Such models are caricatures, not empty illusions: they represent something real but never accurately.",
